          "Carnuntum stood on the Danube, at the frontier of the empire. Pliny measures the distance from here: “From Carnuntum in Pannonia it is about six hundred miles to the coast of Germany from which amber is brought; this was established only recently” (37.45). Six hundred Roman miles is about 890 km.\n\n"
